---
import WindowPage from '../layouts/WindowPage.astro';
import PolicyLinks from '../components/PolicyLinks.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

/*
 * Privacy policy (D35). It describes what the site does today. Update it before any
 * feature that stores visitors' data goes live (likes, comments, accounts, newsletter,
 * analytics), and bump POLICIES.updated in src/lib/site.ts.
 */
const mail = `mailto:${SITE.email}`;
---

<WindowPage
  title="Privacy policy"
  windowTitle="Privacy - Internet Grails"
  description={`What ${SITE.name} collects about visitors (very little) and how to reach us about it.`}
  backHref="/about/"
>
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p>
    The short version: {SITE.name} has no ads and no analytics, and sets no cookies. We know only
    what you choose to give us: a message, or the posts you grail.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} ({SITE.url.replace('https://', '')}) is a website about internet culture. Questions
    about this policy go to <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Messages you send us.</strong> If you use the contact form, we receive your name,
      email address and message. The form is delivered by a form service that passes it to our
      inbox; if it isn't available, the form opens your own email app instead. We use your message
      only to reply and keep it only as long as the conversation needs.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Server logs.</strong> Like every website, our host records basic technical details of
      each request (such as IP address, browser type and the page asked for) to run and protect the
      service. We don't use these to identify you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your grails.</strong> The first time you press <em>Grail it</em>, the site signs you
      in anonymously: you get a random ID with no name or email attached. We store which posts that
      ID grailed and when, so we can show totals and remember yours. Our database provider,
      Supabase, also logs the IP address of each sign-in to protect the service. Grails are stored
      on Supabase's servers in the United States.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We don't sell personal information, and we don't share it except with the services that run the
    site, or when the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      For the current browser tab only, the site remembers that you've already seen the boot screen.
      That note never leaves your device and disappears when you close the tab.
    </li>
    <li>
      Once you've grailed something, your browser keeps your anonymous sign-in in its local storage
      so your grails are still yours next time. Clearing this site's data in your browser forgets
      it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Content from other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Many memes and videos on {SITE.name} are posts from X. Their pictures and videos load straight
    from X's servers, so X receives your IP address when you view them; we don't tell X which page
    you were on. When a post can't be shown that way, or when an article includes a player from X,
    YouTube, Spotify, SoundCloud or TikTok, that company's own code loads on the page and may set
    cookies under its own privacy policy. Links to other sites are covered by those sites' policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} isn't meant for children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect their information.
    If you think a child has sent us personal information, email us and we'll delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us what we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it, by emailing{' '}
    <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a>. You can take back a grail any time by pressing the button
    again. Depending on where you live, you may have further rights under local law; we'll honor
    them.
  </p>

  <h2>Coming soon, and changes</h2>
  <p>
    We plan to add comments, accounts and a newsletter. Before any of those go live, we'll update
    this policy to say what they store and why. When this policy changes, the date below changes
    too.
  </p>

  <PolicyLinks />
</WindowPage>
